payload.answer:
A full plan/inspection handoff for the Marcus/ET reorganization task.

1) Data inventory: 7 sites (1 Fe, 6 O) in site_table; frame_site_order lists 7 entries per frame with consistent label_codes; Cartesian coord arrays are (7,3) and Hessians are (21,21); system_manifest explicitly gives null_rank=6 and resolved_rank=15; medium_response has shell_0_A/shell_1_A/span_A (radii+separation), eps_fast/eps_slow, coupling_eV and temp_K; driving_force_grid has 61 shuffled axis_eV points in [-1.5138, +0.2692]. The "21" in the output shapes is the Cartesian DOF count, not a site count.

2) Reading of site_table.csv and frame_site_order.csv: every frame row maps 1:1 to a unique site_id 0..6 with consistent label_codes; no missing rows; both frames cover all 7 sites. After reordering by argsort(site_id), (site, axis) flat layout gives a 21-vector; no subset trimming needed.

3) Proposed approach:
   (a) COM-translate, plain-Cartesian Kabsch aligning B onto A (forward) and A onto B (backward), preserving signed source-minus-reference-target convention;
   (b) build per-DOF mass vector from site masses repeated 3x per site, build mass-weighted Hessian H_mw = M^{-1/2} H M^{-1/2} after re-permuting H to ascending site_id;
   (c) diagonalise H_mw, drop 6 zero (rigid) modes, keep 15 positive-eigenvalue eigenvectors sorted by ascending frequency (matches contract shape (2,21,15) and system_manifest);
   (d) aligned_displacement_mw = M^{1/2}·(aligned-source − reference-target) flat; projected_displacement_mw = V V^T d_mw;
   (e) mode_overlap = |⟨ψ_A_i|ψ_B'_j⟩| (B' rotated to A's frame); magnitude-based throughout per contract; transported_mode_projection and mode_projection defined column by column in the plan;
   (f) 4-point formula 0.5·d^T H d for λ_4pt (per Hessian); λ_nm = sum of 0.5·q_j^2·ω_j^2 over retained modes; λ_inner_eff = 0.5·(λ_4pt_fwd + λ_4pt_bwd); λ_outer via Marcus two-sphere with e^2/4πε_0 = 14.3996 eV·Å; rate via Marcus-Levich-Dogonadze non-adiabatic expression k_et = (2π/ℏ)·|V|^2·(4πλkBT)^(-1/2)·exp[-(λ+ΔG)^2/(4λkBT)]; k_self_exchange reported at ΔG = -λ_total (barrier-zero, finite prefactor); inverted-region rule documented.

4) Assumptions and uncertainties explicitly enumerated (A1-A17 in the plan body). Most consequential: (A1) 21 = 7 sites × 3 Cartesian DOFs (not 21 sites); (A2) plain-Cartesian Kabsch alignment; (A4) Marcus two-sphere outer-sphere formula; (A6) Marcus-Levich-Dogonadze non-adiabatic rate; (A8) first_inverted_grid_id = first CSV-row-order entry with axis_eV < -λ_total; (A13) column semantics of mode_projection (2,15,3) and transported_mode_projection (2,15,2); (A15) matplotlib unavailable - render overview.png via stdlib PNG encoder.

Diagnostics observables from a dry run: mass-weighted Kabsch-aligned displacement has norm ~33.6 (amu^0.5*A); naive lambda_inner estimates using H_A and H_B raw give ~0.40 eV and ~1.64 eV respectively, so lambda_inner_eff ≈ 1.02 eV, lambda_outer ≈ 0.734 eV, lambda_total ≈ 1.75 eV; rate peak lies at ΔG ≈ -1.75 eV, just past the lower end of the [-1.514, +0.269] eV grid, so inverted region will be detected over most of the supplied grid.

No analysis.py / no output files written. Awaiting approach_review.

